0},{"id":13,"traceSequence":15,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"list\" \"--state\" \"open\" \"--limit\" \"1\" \"--head\" \"fix/420-oxc-sigill-downgrade\" \"--json\" \"number,url\"","status":"done","output":"[]\n","code":0},{"id":14,"traceSequence":16,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"create\" \"--title\" \"Pin oxfmt 0.79.0 and oxlint 1.94.0 to avoid SIGILL on CPUs without BMI2\" \"--body\" \"Refs #420, oxc-project/oxc#30164.\\n\\noxfmt 0.80.0 and oxlint 1.95.0 ship `linux-x64-gnu` bindings built by GCC 15.2, which defaults to `-march=x86-64-v3`, so they contain BMI2 instructions. They crash with SIGILL on x86-64 CPUs without BMI2 (pre-Haswell).\\n\\n| binding | BMI1/BMI2 instructions (objdump) | compiler |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| @oxfmt/binding-linux-x64-gnu 0.80.0 | 150 | GCC 15.2 (Ubuntu 26.04) |\\n| @oxlint/binding-linux-x64-gnu 1.95.0 | 150 | GCC 15.2 (Ubuntu 26.04) |\\n| @oxfmt/binding-linux-x64-gnu 0.79.0 | 0 | GCC 13.3 (Ubuntu 24.04) |\\n| @oxlint/binding-linux-x64-gnu 1.94.0 | 0 | GCC 13.3 (Ubuntu 24.04) |\\n\\noxfmt is a runtime dependency (`src/tool/source-formatter.ts`), so this affects users, not only contributors.\\n\\n- Pins `oxfmt` to 0.79.0 and `oxlint` to 1.94.0 (exact versions).\\n- Has Dependabot ignore only the broken versions. Newer releases will still be proposed, and each one should be checked for BMI2 instructions before merging.\\n- Adds a changelog entry.\\n\\n`delivery.validate()` passes: check and tests.\" \"--base\" \"main\" \"--head\" \"fix/420-oxc-sigill-downgrade\"","status":"done","output":"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/421\n","code":0}],"traces":[{"id":1,"sequence":1,"namespace":"__pit","method":"savedFunctionRun","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":24}],"startedAt":1795574475523,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":1,"name":"delivery.openPullRequest","scope":"project","depth":1},"durationMs":0},{"id":2,"sequence":2,"namespace":"shell","method":"execFile","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":3},{"type":"array","size":3},{"type":"object","